## Context

Five of the eight sources have no test file (crossref, unpaywall, hal, libgen, url). The sources that
fail in practice are scrapers whose upstream changes without notice (ticket 0001 retargeted Sci-Hub).

## Actions
1. One parametrised conformance suite run against every source of 0008's registry: success, not found,
   HTTP error, timeout, non-PDF body; each must yield the contract's result and leave no partial file.
2. Per-source tests on recorded HTTP responses (saved fixtures, no network) for the parsing each
   scraper does.
3. The `network` tests stay out of the gate; run them periodically on the author's machine (a /lair or
   /molt step, or a local timer), a red there being a drift signal for a fix ticket.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Every registered source passes the conformance suite
- [ ] Each source has at least one fixture-based parsing test
- [ ] Offline suite stays under a few seconds and inside 0007's gate
